$$\sim_a \sqrt{n} \tilde{\gamma}_j - \mathbb{E}(\mathbf{x}_{t-j} \cdot \varepsilon_t + \mathbf{x}_t \cdot \varepsilon_{t-j})' \sqrt{n} (\mathbf{b} - \boldsymbol{\beta})$$

$$(\text{since } \frac{1}{n} \sum_{t=j+1}^n (\mathbf{x}_{t-j} \cdot \varepsilon_t + \mathbf{x}_t \cdot \varepsilon_{t-j}) \rightarrow_{\text{p}} \text{E}(\mathbf{x}_{t-j} \cdot \varepsilon_t + \mathbf{x}_t \cdot \varepsilon_{t-j}))$$

$$= \sqrt{n}\tilde{\gamma}_j - \mu'_j\sqrt{n}(\mathbf{b} - \boldsymbol{\beta}) \quad \text{where } \boldsymbol{\mu}_j \equiv E(\mathbf{x}_t \cdot \boldsymbol{\varepsilon}_{t-j})$$

(since 
$$E(\mathbf{x}_{t-j} \cdot \boldsymbol{\varepsilon}_t) = \mathbf{0}$$
