- 3. Let **SSR** be the sum of squared residuals defined in (5.2.15). For the errorcomponent model with the spherical assumption that E(qi q:) = **a; IM,** prove

$$\lim_{n \rightarrow \infty} \frac{SSR}{n} = (M - 1) \cdot \sigma_{\eta}^2.$$

**Hint:** 

$$\begin{aligned}
 SSR &= \sum_{i=1}^n [\mathbf{Q}(\mathbf{y}_i - \mathbf{F}_i \hat{\boldsymbol{\beta}}_{\text{FE}})]' [\mathbf{Q}(\mathbf{y}_i - \mathbf{F}_i \hat{\boldsymbol{\beta}}_{\text{FE}})] \\
 &= \sum_{i=1}^n (\mathbf{y}_i - \mathbf{F}_i \hat{\boldsymbol{\beta}}_{\text{FE}})' \mathbf{Q}(\mathbf{y}_i - \mathbf{F}_i \hat{\boldsymbol{\beta}}_{\text{FE}}) \\
 &\quad \text{(since } \mathbf{Q} \text{ is symmetric and idempotent)} \\
 &= \sum_{i=1}^n (\mathbf{y}_i - \mathbf{F}_i \hat{\boldsymbol{\beta}}_{\text{FE}})' \mathbf{C}(\mathbf{C}'\mathbf{C})^{-1} \mathbf{C}' (\mathbf{y}_i - \mathbf{F}_i \hat{\boldsymbol{\beta}}_{\text{FE}}) \quad \text{(by (11))} \\
 &= \sum_{i=1}^n \hat{\mathbf{v}}'_i (\mathbf{C}'\mathbf{C})^{-1} \hat{\mathbf{v}}_i \quad (\hat{\mathbf{v}}_i \equiv \mathbf{C}'\mathbf{y}_i - \mathbf{C}'\mathbf{F}_i \hat{\boldsymbol{\beta}}_{\text{FE}}) \\
 &= \sum_{i=1}^n \text{trace}[\hat{\mathbf{v}}'_i (\mathbf{C}'\mathbf{C})^{-1} \hat{\mathbf{v}}_i] \\
 &= \sum_{i=1}^n \text{trace}[(\mathbf{C}'\mathbf{C})^{-1} \hat{\mathbf{v}}_i \hat{\mathbf{v}}'_i] \\
 &= n \cdot \text{trace} \left[ (\mathbf{C}'\mathbf{C})^{-1} \frac{1}{n} \sum_{i=1}^n \hat{\mathbf{v}}_i \hat{\mathbf{v}}'_i \right] \quad \text{(since the trace operator is linear).}
 \end{aligned}$$

