As we know from the theory of homogeneous difference equations (summarized in Analytical Exercise 4), the solution sequence {+;} to (6.1.17) eventually starts declining at a geometric rate if what is known as the stability **condition**  holds. The condition states:

All the roots of the p-th degree polynomial equation in z

$$\phi(z) = 0 \quad \text{where} \quad \phi(z) \equiv 1 - \phi_1 z - \phi_2 z^2 - \dots - \phi_p z^p \quad (6.1.18)$$

