**Hint:** If x, is as in Proposition 6.7, then

$$E(\mathbf{x}_i, \mathbf{x}'_i) = \begin{bmatrix} 1 & \mu \mathbf{1}' \\ \mu \mathbf{1} & \mathbf{V} + \mu^2 \mathbf{1}\mathbf{1}' \end{bmatrix},$$

where 1 is a p x 1 vector of ones. Show that the inverse of this matrix is

